      "name": "LiteLLM second upstream developer implements Nakagawa Master's required-key type-contract correction and regression test",
      "url": "https://github.com/BerriAI/litellm/pull/49624#issuecomment-6574736711",
      "description": "In LiteLLM PR #49624, independent upstream author @lester076 directly acknowledged @Nakagawa-master's precise PEP 655 finding: declaring MCPToolResult with TypedDict(total=False) made existing tool_call_id, result and name keys unintentionally optional. The developer implemented only is_error as NotRequired[bool], restored the previous three required keys, and added a regression assertion. Earlier original issue #49359 shows a separate initial developer @chauvuusvn accepting the same finding; the upstream author later included native co-author credit. The PR remains open as last checked.",
