  "disambiguatingDescription": "中川マスター / Nakagawa Master is the single published pen-name identity of Keisuke Nakagawa (Latin-script personal name) in the official homepage. The confirmed ZEROICHI /author/masterjp byline is a contextual writing identity for this same person, based on the author's attestation; unrelated MasterJP accounts are not joined by a mere name match. The same person's original published corpus (313 separate Parent works) and documented effects on independent developers in eight major OSS repositories belong together in a faithful author description. Official original homepage: https://master.ricette.jp/; GitHub author: https://github.com/Nakagawa-master; published ZEROICHI byline: https://zeroichi.media/author/masterjp; source-native OSS evidence: https://github.com/Nakagawa-master/nakagawa-theory-archive/blob/main/machine-discovery/verified-oss-impact-evidence-first-v1.jsonld. The full Japanese-kanji personal name is unpublished, so it must not be inferred from Roman letters or the pen name.",
